data.content:
It works. Here's the full program:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase
};

var person = new Person("Alice", 30);
Console.WriteLine(JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options));

public record Person(string name, int age);
```

**Output:**
```json
{"Name":"Alice","Age":30}
```

.NET 11 adds a built-in `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` policy, so `name` → `Name` and `age` → `Age` with no custom code needed. The project targets `net11.0`.
